"""Real composer captures at the shadow pane widths (t2280).

Captured 2026-11-12 by the t2280 measurement spike (two runs) on a throwaway tmux server
(tmux 3.8, ``-f /dev/null``, one single-pane session per agent and width,
W x 30) from claude 2.1.322, codex-cli 0.167.2 and opencode 1.18.34, at W = 60
(``shadow_pane_width``'s default) and W = 44, at the extent production reads
(``capture-pane -p -e -S -15``). Text was typed with ``send-keys -l``, the
path the minimonitor's recheck uses. Never trim these: a dropped row can be a
load-bearing delimiter (``capture_raw_tail``'s docstring).

Every capture follows one warm-up turn ("Reply with the single word OK"), so
the composer is in the conversation layout a rechecking shadow is always in
(for opencode the full-width box, not the centred home box).

Each entry: ``(agent, pane_width, shadow_state at capture time, request, raw)``,
the same shape as ``sitrep_request_fixtures.FIXTURES``.

Names are ``<agent>_w<W>_<variant>`` and are a stable interface: t2275 renders
its minimonitor test fake's composer from them. Variants:

* ``recheck_plan`` / ``recheck_impl`` / ``recheck_generic`` -- the real
  ``review_loop.compose_recheck_prompt(phase, 1)`` for phase PLAN, IMPLEMENT
  and None, in the composer;
* ``appended`` -- the PLAN prompt, then " plus my own words" typed after it
  (request = the PLAN prompt);
* ``history_draft`` -- "an unrelated draft of mine" in the composer, the
  warm-up request in the history (request = the warm-up request);
* ``edge_<k>_<total>`` -- ``"a"*k + " " + "b"*w + " tail"`` with
  ``k + 1 + w = total`` at the wrap width - 1, the wrap width and + 1;
* ``hyphen_<k>_<p>`` -- ``"a"*k + " " + "b"*m + "-" + "c"*10 + " tail"`` with
  the hyphen-ended prefix ``k + 1 + m + 1 = p`` around each agent's hyphen
  break bound (opencode also at content width + 1);
* ``midtoken`` -- ``">q c12 "`` + one unbroken token of 3 x W letters (hard
  breaks: the only rows that measure the content width);
* ``post_enter`` -- the generic prompt submitted, captured 0.5 s after Enter
  (claude / codex read ``working``; opencode already reads ``ready``);
* ``endword_<k>_<total>`` / ``endhyphen_<k>_<total>`` -- a text that ENDS in the
  piece that may move: ``"a"*k + " " + "b"*w`` / ``"a"*k + "-" + "b"*w``, total
  length at the content width - 1, the content width and + 1. Every agent
  keeps a final piece on the row up to the content width itself. At exactly the
  content width codex moves its cursor onto an empty row, which no grammar can
  tell from a typed blank line, so those two captures are UNPROVABLE
  (``composer_payload`` returns None) -- by measurement, not by omission.

``opencode_w120_end*`` are a supplement at 120 columns (conversation layout),
recorded because they correct a synthetic 120-column assertion in
tests/test_sitrep_request_delivery.py; ``WIDTHS`` lists only the fully covered
shadow widths.

The plan's "Measurement" section (aiplans/archived/p2280_*.md) records what
these showed. Scrubbed: the agents ran in a neutral ``/tmp/ait_t2280_*/proj``
directory, and every capture was checked for the user name, home path,
hostname, git name and email local parts -- none occurred, so nothing was
substituted.
"""

